  nodeConstituents: 06000000
  nodePositions: []
  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: What is GLP-1R's structure?
    basic: 'GLP-1R has three parts: the extracellular domain, transmembrane domain
      and intracellular domain.'
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "GLP-1R is a class B secretin GPCR that conserves many characteristics
      in the family. \nIt spans the plasma membrane via a 7-helix transmembrane bundle.
      \nA large N-terminal extracellular domain is critical for ligand recognition
      and binding. \nIt also has an intracellular helix at the C terminus."
  - title: What is GLP-1R's extracellular domain?
    basic: "The extracellular domain is outside the cell and is connected to the
      transmembrane domain. \nIt moves and tilts and can affect how and if certain
      molecular structures bind to GLP-1R"
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: What is GLP-1R's transmembrane domain?
    basic: "The transmembrane domain is a bundle of 7 helices that are embedded in
      the membrane. \nThey ensure GLP-1R stays on the membrane and receives signals
      from outside of the cell"
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  - title: What is GLP-1R's intracellular domain?
    basic: 'The intracellular domain is the part of GLP-1R that faces the cell interior.

      Under
      certain conditions it provides a binding pocket for nearby G proteins'
    intermediate: 
    advanced: 
  nodeSpriteLayer: []
